# Devcontainer environment files.
# devcontainer.env is generated on the host by .devcontainer/sync-common.sh from
# devcontainer.env.example, and may hold machine-specific values (proxies etc.),
# so it is not tracked. The .example template IS tracked - docker fails hard when
# --env-file points at a missing file, so the template must survive a fresh clone.
# site.env is also tracked: it holds this project's shared-devcontainer config
# (deployment suffix, version fallbacks) and contains no secrets.
.devcontainer/devcontainer.env

# Custom CA certificates are site-specific and must not be committed to this
# public repo. CA handling was removed from the shared layer; if a project needs
# a private CA, add it in that project's own .devcontainer/Dockerfile layer.
*.crt
